## System Summary

`adversarial-spec` is a file-backed, multi-model specification workflow: a debate CLI and gauntlet create concerns and verdicts; strict validation/TMR tools produce evidence-backed close artifacts; hooks independently protect tooling and coordinate with Fizzy.

## Quick Start

- **Primer first:** [primer.md](primer.md) is the small-context entrypoint.
- **Fix first:** [concerns.md](concerns.md) is the actionable rollup.
- **Navigation only:** this page routes readers; it is not a substitute for contracts or flows.
- **Guided reading:** [access-guide.md](access-guide.md).

## Components

| Component | Purpose | Runtime | Architecture | Key Files |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Debate and session | pipeline-gated critique/resume | implemented | active_primary | `debate.py`, `session.py` |
| Models and providers | adapter/rate/cost routing | implemented | active_primary | `models.py`, `providers.py` |
| Gauntlet orchestration | seven-phase concern verdict | implemented | active_primary | `gauntlet/orchestrator.py` |
| Gauntlet persistence | checkpoint/run artifacts | implemented | active_primary | `gauntlet/persistence.py` |
| Pre-gauntlet | repository grounding/alignment | implemented | active_primary | `pre_gauntlet/` |
| Validation emission | ledger/evidence/human judgment | implemented | active_primary | `validation_emission.py` |
| TMR and provenance | strict registry/transition proof | implemented | active_primary | `tmr_schema.py`, `provenance_journal.py` |
| Hook plane | safety and notification adapters | implemented | active_primary | `.claude/hooks/` |
| Plan analysis | concern/dependency analysis | partial | active_secondary | `execution_planner/`, `dependency_semantics.py` |
| Telegram and usage | human channel/headroom route | implemented | active_secondary | `telegram_bot.py`, `usage_router.py` |

## Navigation

| Intent | Read |
|---|---|
| Understand system | [primer.md](primer.md) then [overview.md](overview.md) |
| Fix first | [concerns.md](concerns.md) |
| Evaluate a plan | primer -> matching [component](structured/components/) -> [cross-references](structured/cross-references.md) |
| Change debate/model routing | `debate-session.md`, `models-providers.md`, then [flows](structured/flows.md) |
| Change gauntlet behavior | `gauntlet-orchestration.md`, `gauntlet-persistence.md`, then [flows](structured/flows.md) |
| Change validation/TMR closeout | `validation-emission.md`, `tmr-provenance.md`, then [cross-references](structured/cross-references.md) |
| Change a hook | `harness-hooks.md`, then [cross-references](structured/cross-references.md) |

## Architecture Decisions

- **Typed contracts + file evidence:** resume and closeout paths use explicit dataclasses/schema/hash bindings.
- **Provider-bounded concurrency:** parallel model work is grouped/rate-limited by provider.
- **Process-separated hooks:** hook behavior consumes JSON and emits side effects without runtime imports.
- **Source-over-doc trust:** the dirty worktree makes this corpus caution-grade until source is committed or remapped.

